course: dictionary
lesson: 9091
title: A word with a hard history: slum
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe a place, and the words around them tell you how that place feels. «About a billion people live in informal settlements, often called slums, mostly because cities grow faster than proper homes, pipes and roads can be built.» The clues are cities growing fast, homes not built properly, and people living without roads or pipes. So a slum is a place where people are poor and homes are badly built.
explain: The word slum can also be informal, which means it is used in everyday talk. If someone says, «Your bedroom is a slum!», they do not mean a city district. They mean the room is very messy and dirty. Check the sentence: if you put "very messy room" in its place, it still makes sense.
explain: Slum can be a verb too. To slum it means to live somewhere cheaper or less comfortable than you are used to, often for a short time. Words like this come in phrases, so look at the words beside them, such as slum landlord, which means a landlord who rents out bad, unsafe homes.
fact: A slum is a very poor, crowded part of a city where houses are badly built.
fact: Many slums lack clean water, toilets and safe electricity.
fact: «Slum» can also mean a very messy, dirty room or house, in informal talk.
fact: «Slum it» means to live somewhere less comfortable than usual, often for a short time.
fact: In Victorian London and in big cities today, slums grew when cities grew faster than homes could be built.
exercise: «About a billion people live in informal settlements, often called slums.» What is a slum? | A quiet village in the countryside | A big shopping centre in the middle of town | A very tall office block | *A very poor, crowded part of a city with badly built homes
exercise: «Your bedroom is a slum!» What does this mean? | A tidy room with clean floors | A room with a big bed and a bright window | *A very messy, dirty room | A room that is always cold in winter
exercise: Find and copy one word from «About a billion people live in informal settlements, often called slums.» that means not official or not formally arranged. | *informal | slums | billion | settlements
test: Jade says, «We can slum it in a tent this weekend instead of a hotel.» What does slum it mean? | Visit a famous city and see its palaces | Win a prize for being the tidiest camper | Build a house out of wood and stone | *Stay somewhere simpler and less comfortable than usual
test: Which phrase means a landlord who rents out bad, unsafe homes? | *slum landlord | slum dunk | slum it | slum clearance
exam: Why do slums often grow in fast-growing cities? | *Because cities grow faster than proper homes, pipes and roads can be built | Because governments build too many parks | Because slums are the cheapest places to visit | Because people prefer small, dark houses
